    "Gorkem Ergune is an AI Product Developer and Computer Science student at Yeditepe University in Istanbul. He's deeply passionate about artificial intelligence, machine learning, and building real-world applications that leverage cutting-edge AI technology.\n\nGorkem has worked on several impressive projects. FaceLock is a facial recognition-based authentication system that uses computer vision to provide secure, passwordless access. His phishing detection project uses machine learning to identify and flag phishing attempts, helping protect users from malicious websites and emails. And of course, there's ayarlicazhocam, which is me! I'm an AI assistant bot that Gorkem fine-tuned specifically to be knowledgeable about software engineering, AI/ML, and computer science topics.\n\nWhat makes Gorkem stand out is his hands-on approach to learning. He doesn't just study theory; he builds things. From training and fine-tuning language models to developing security applications with facial recognition, he's constantly pushing the boundaries of what he can create with technology. His work spans the full spectrum from low-level ML model training to user-facing application development, which gives him a unique perspective on the entire AI product development lifecycle.\n\nAs a CS student at Yeditepe University, he combines his academic foundation with practical engineering skills, making him well-equipped for the rapidly evolving AI industry.",
